CoreCLR on riscv64 (plan step V2.4): upstream turns W^X off by default on riscv64 (dotnet/runtime issue 103465), so the executable allocator commits code pages as writable and executable at once, which WitOS never grants (plain memory never executes; a JIT writes through the RW view of a double mapping and the RX view is published): the commit of the write barrier copy in InitThreadManager failed, the copy wrote into the reserved page and corerun ended with a fault before the runtime had installed its handlers. The default stays on for WitOS, on riscv64 as on x64 and ARM64; a TARGET_WITOS branch beside the platform's own (RFC 0015 section 4), since the knob exists and WitOS has one mode.

--- a/src/coreclr/inc/clrconfigvalues.h
+++ b/src/coreclr/inc/clrconfigvalues.h
@@ -639,11 +639,12 @@
 // Executable code
 //
 // TODO: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/103465
-#ifdef TARGET_RISCV64
+// WitOS never grants writable executable memory, so W^X is the one mode there, on riscv64 as on the other ISAs.
+#if defined(TARGET_RISCV64) && !defined(TARGET_WITOS)
 RETAIL_CONFIG_DWORD_INFO(EXTERNAL_EnableWriteXorExecute, W("EnableWriteXorExecute"), 0, "Enable W^X for executable memory.");
 #else
 RETAIL_CONFIG_DWORD_INFO(EXTERNAL_EnableWriteXorExecute, W("EnableWriteXorExecute"), 1, "Enable W^X for executable memory.");
-#endif // TARGET_RISCV64
+#endif // TARGET_RISCV64 && !TARGET_WITOS
 
